        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 50,
        "headingId": 371,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8474/1 Seromucinous borderline tumour</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T16:52:15"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 459,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 372,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61748,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 50,
        "headingId": 372,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2C73.Y &amp; XH0RB9 Other specified malignant neoplasms of the ovary &amp; Seromucinous borderline tumour</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T16:52:15"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 460,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 373,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61749,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 50,
        "headingId": 373,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> endocervical-type mucinous borderline tumour; M&uuml;llerian mucinous borderline tumour</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T16:52:15"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 461,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 374,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61750,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 50,
        "headingId": 374,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T16:52:15"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61751,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 50,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Ovary</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T16:52:15"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61752,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 50,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours present over a wide age range (mean age: 34&ndash;39&nbsp;years) {3338022; 3334969; 12459620; 15371946}. Patients typically present with symptoms related to a pelvic mass, or the mass may be an incidental finding on imaging.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T16:52:15"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61753,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 50,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Seromucinous borderline tumours are uncommon ovarian neoplasms {3338022; 3334969}. A significant number of patients have associated endometriosis, most commonly an endometriotic cyst (31&ndash;35%) {12459620; 15371946}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T16:52:15"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61754,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 50,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Many seromucinous borderline tumours arise from endometriotic cysts.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T16:52:15"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61755,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 50,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "<p>Loss of ARID1A expression, a surrogate for <em>ARID1A</em> mutations, has been reported in one&nbsp;third of these tumours&nbsp;&ndash; a frequency similar to that seen in endometrioid neoplasms, supporting their close relationship {22653341}. <em>KRAS</em> mutations are often present (found in 69% of tumours) {20955384}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-02T17:51:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61756,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 50,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Seromucinous borderline tumours are usually confined to the ovary, typically with a smooth outer surface. As many as 30% are bilateral {12459620}. The mean tumour size is 9&nbsp;cm {12459620}. The tumours typically comprise a unilocular cyst with friable papillary excrescences involving the inner cyst lining. Solid areas are occasionally seen.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T16:52:15"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61757,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 50,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Seromucinous borderline tumours are composed of papillae exhibiting hierarchical branching, with variably oedematous or fibrous stromal cores {3338022; 3334969; 12459620; 15371946}. Larger papillae tend to have a swollen oedematous stroma containing conspicuous neutrophils. The epithelium lining the papillae is cytologically bland, stratified, and often tufted. It represents an admixture of M&uuml;llerian cell types in varying proportions, including endometrioid (with foci of squamous and mucinous differentiation&nbsp;/ endocervical-type mucinous), ciliated, hobnail, clear, and indifferent (nondescript) eosinophilic cells. Sometimes, mucinous differentiation greatly predominates. Microinvasion has been described {12459620; 15371946}. A portion of the cyst lining may exhibit features of an endometriotic cyst. The epithelial cells are generally positive with PAX8, ER, and PR and usually WT1-negative; p53 exhibits wildtype immunoreactivity {26598986}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T16:52:15"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61758,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 50,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T16:52:15"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61759,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 50,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T16:52:15"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61760,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 50,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> papillae exhibiting hierarchical branching with oedematous and fibrous stromal cores lined by an admixture of M&uuml;llerian cell types exhibiting proliferation, but without stromal invasion.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> evidence of endometriosis.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T16:52:15"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61761,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 50,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "<p>Seromucinous borderline tumour is staged according to the Union for International Cancer Control (UICC) TNM classification (see <em>TNM staging of ovarian, fallopian tube, and primary peritoneal carcinoma</em>&nbsp;[[Brierley JD, Gospodarowicz MK, Wittekind C, editors. TNM classification of malignant tumours. 8th ed. Oxford (UK): Wiley-Blackwell; 2017.]]) and the FIGO staging system.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-15T11:07:42"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61762,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 50,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The prognosis is excellent. Malignant behaviour has not been reported in well-documented cases {12459620; 15371946}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T16:52:15"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]